Z||000002||JetroGT||12-10-1999||04:51 AM||||That depends if you want to drive cramed up against the steering wheel. I used to have 10 inch MTX subs in boxes behind the seats in my 86 2M4 when I was in high school. Very uncomfortable.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||12-10-1999||10:53 PM||||I have a single 8 inch JBL GT series sub (around $60 from Crutchfield), mounted in a .5 cubic foot sealed box behind the passenger's seat, with my amp (250 watt bridged Kenwood) and crossover behind my seat mounted on a board.  It'll change your heart rhythm with the windows up and the roof in.  My 5 year old son doesn't mind sitting all the way up on his side.  He's closer to the controls that way.  The box is covered in matching grey cloth, so it looks like a package tray.  I'll post the box dimensions if anybody wants them.||||reg||1
